          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fd629cfcacd3287fde9f30f9feaa5931aa854b77",
          "message": "fix(ci): unpatchable Dependabot advisories no longer red the main gate (#3768)\n\nThe gate classified non-gating check-runs purely by NAME token\n(`\\b(advisory|informational)\\b`, `is_advisory()`). That rule can only reach\ncheck-runs whose name THIS repo controls — a GitHub-MANAGED job's name is\nchosen by GitHub, so it can never carry the token, and it therefore GATED.\n\nLive defect: main gate run 30136978362 (2026-07-25T00:46Z) failed fast on\n`- ✗ Dependabot: failure` as the ONLY gating failure, and so did the previous\nmain gate run 30131008188 (2026-07-24T22:29Z). The underlying job (Dependabot\nUpdates run 30136987253) concluded `security_update_not_possible` for npm\n`brace-expansion`: a patched release exists (5.0.8, the only version outside\nthe `<= 5.0.7` affected range) but `minimatch@3.1.5`'s `^1.1.7` pin caps the\nreachable path at 1.1.16, so Dependabot correctly reports it cannot act. An\nupstream condition with no in-repo remedy was tripping the stop-the-line rule.\n(The merge queue was NOT blocked — PR #3764 merged at 00:44 during that red —\nso the cost was false alarm + telemetry noise, not stalled merges.)\n\nFix: a documented, EXACT, fail-closed allow-list\n(`PLATFORM_MANAGED_ADVISORY_NAMES` / `is_platform_managed_advisory()`) beside\nthe existing name-token rule. Whole-name case-insensitive match only — no\nsubstring/prefix/wildcard — so an unknown or renamed platform check still\nGATES; widening it is always a reviewed edit. The only entry is \"Dependabot\",\nverified against the Actions Jobs API over the newest 60 runs of workflow\n294954269 (`dynamic/dependabot/dependabot-updates`): the ONLY job name it has\never emitted is exactly \"Dependabot\" (37 success / 23 failure), and no\nrepo-authored workflow declares a job of that name.\n\n`is_advisory()` stays the SINGLE non-gating classifier so all three consumers\ninherit one answer — the verdict, fail-fast, and the resolver's run-level\nsynthetic check (`advisory_only_failure`). Splitting them would let the red\nDependabot workflow run acquire a synthetic gating verdict and red the gate\nanyway.\n\nSecurity posture unchanged: nothing is suppressed. The Dependabot alert stays\nopen, Dependabot keeps retrying and will open the PR the moment a reachable\npatch exists, and the actionable cargo dependency-vulnerability GATE\n(`cargo deny check advisories` inside `supply-chain gates (…)`) is untouched.\nHonest caveat: that lane covers the cargo graph; there is no in-repo npm\nvulnerability gate today, so Dependabot alerts remain the npm surveillance\nsurface — which is why this must not, and does not, touch alerting. The\nadvisory is TRACKED in #3767 (a VEX record is structurally unavailable:\n`supply-chain/vex.cdx.json` is held in set equality with `deny.toml\n[advisories].ignore` by the gating `check-vex-deny-drift.py`, so an npm GHSA\nthere would red that check).\n\nTests: 7 new cases — exactly \"Dependabot\" failing does not red the verdict;\nunknown/new names still RED (fail-closed) at both predicate and verdict level;\nthe pre-existing advisory-name rule (incl. plural \"advisories\" gating) intact;\na real gating failure alongside a Dependabot failure still REDs and is what\nthe verdict blames; no fail-fast on a Dependabot red; and no synthetic\nrun-level gating verdict for a Dependabot-only workflow failure. 127/127 green.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
